        "reason": "The outcome holds the expected result. All three inputs encode MALK*. All 39 variants pass the protein and length gates. The first sequence scores 41.6249 in the baseline step, using the same ostir_expression settings as the candidates. beats_reference kept 22 variants scoring 46.93 or 50.84, all strictly above it. It sent 17 variants to the no branch, including 14d99e9ca59d, which ties at 41.6249, so ties and lower scores were excluded. Coverage is weaker. The better assertions (higher_initiation_rate, only_improved_kept) are only 'produced', which shows the filter kept something, not that every kept score beats the baseline. The yes-branch assertion that would show this was not made, and only_improved_kept names the no branch but never checks it. The protein assertion is also only 'produced'. The protein_ok filter threshold of 1.0 and the all-1.0 columns do show that every variant passed. However, the check compares against the first sequence only, not each variant's own input, which is harmless here since all three inputs share one protein. The DNA alphabet is guaranteed by the type. I verified the scores by reading them, not through any assertion. Stop codons and the start codon were not asserted: stops vary among TAA, TAG and TGA, which is synonymous, and ATG is untouched.\n\nAcceptance: the verifier judged the assertions not to cover the goal",
